---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '@/components/SiteFooter.astro';
import SupportingPage from '@/components/SupportingPage.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use | SpellingWords"
  description="Read the plain-language terms for using SpellingWords educational content, spelling practice, custom lists, and shared links."
>
  <SiteHeader currentPath="/terms" />
  <SupportingPage
    eyebrow="Terms"
    title="Terms of Use"
    intro="These terms set reasonable ground rules for using the free educational content and browser-based practice tools on SpellingWords.app."
    currentPath="/terms"
  >
    <section aria-labelledby="acceptance-heading">
      <h2 id="acceptance-heading">Using SpellingWords</h2>
      <p>
        By using SpellingWords, you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do not agree, please do not
        use the site. A parent, guardian, teacher, or other responsible adult should guide a child's
        use when appropriate.
      </p>
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> August 25, 2026</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="purpose-heading">
      <h2 id="purpose-heading">Educational purpose</h2>
      <p>
        SpellingWords provides supplemental K–5 spelling references, word lists, and practice. It is
        not a replacement for a teacher's judgment, individualized instruction, a school's adopted
        curriculum, or professional educational advice. Grade labels are useful starting points, but
        schools and learners may introduce or revisit spelling concepts at different times.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="permitted-heading">
      <h2 id="permitted-heading">Reasonable use</h2>
      <p>
        You may use the site for personal, family, classroom, tutoring, and homeschool learning. You
        may share links to public pages and use the site's ordinary browser features with students.
        These permissions do not transfer ownership of the site or allow republishing substantial
        portions of its original content as another product or website.
      </p>
      <p>You may not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>break the law or violate another person's rights through the site;</li>
        <li>probe, bypass, or interfere with site security or normal operation;</li>
        <li>send malicious code or use automation that unreasonably burdens the service;</li>
        <li>
          misrepresent SpellingWords content as your own product or official school requirement;
        </li>
        <li>
          use custom lists or shared links to distribute harmful, unlawful, or private personal
          information.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="lists-heading">
      <h2 id="lists-heading">Custom word lists and shared links</h2>
      <p>
        You are responsible for the words and optional titles you enter. Do not include a child's
        name, contact details, school information, or other private information. SpellingWords does
        not review or endorse user-created list content.
      </p>
      <p>
        Anyone with a complete shared-list link can see and use its contents. You are responsible
        for deciding what a link contains and who receives it. Shared links are encoded, not
        encrypted, and are not guaranteed to remain available or compatible forever as browsers and
        the service change.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ownership-heading">
      <h2 id="ownership-heading">Site content and intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The site's original explanations, curriculum organization, interface, visual design, and
        software are protected by applicable intellectual-property laws. Individual spelling words,
        general facts, and ideas are not claimed as exclusive property merely because they appear on
        the site. Third-party material remains the property of its respective owner.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="services-heading">
      <h2 id="services-heading">Browser and third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The site depends on browsers, devices, hosting, fonts, and browser speech-synthesis services
        that SpellingWords does not fully control. Available voices, pronunciation, network
        behavior, accessibility support, and service availability can vary. External links lead to
        sites with their own terms and policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="availability-heading">
      <h2 id="availability-heading">Availability, changes, and accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        SpellingWords may correct, add, remove, or reorganize content and features. The site may
        sometimes be unavailable, and no particular page, list, shared-link format, or feature is
        promised permanently.
      </p>
      <p>
        Reasonable care is taken with educational content, but errors may occur. Pronunciation,
        dialect, curriculum expectations, and individual learning needs also vary. Parents and
        educators should use their judgment when deciding whether particular content or practice is
        appropriate for a learner.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="disclaimer-heading">
      <h2 id="disclaimer-heading">No warranty and reasonable limits</h2>
      <p>
        SpellingWords is provided free of charge on an “as available” basis, without a promise that
        it will always be uninterrupted, error-free, or suitable for every learner or curriculum. To
        the extent permitted by applicable law, SpellingWords and its operator will not be liable
        for indirect, incidental, special, or consequential losses arising from use of—or inability
        to use—the site. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or responsibilities that cannot
        lawfully be excluded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="changes-heading">
      <h2 id="changes-heading">Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        These terms may be updated as the service changes. The current version will be posted here
        with a revised “Last updated” date. Continued use after an update means the new terms apply
        to later use of the site.
      </p>
    </section>
  </SupportingPage>
  <SiteFooter />
</Layout>
